# Persian and RTL

- Use `react-intl` messages; do not embed new user-facing copy directly in components.
- Add canonical English and Persian entries together, following nearby namespaces. SafeMeet-specific keys should use `app.skyroom.*` where appropriate.
- Do not edit generated locale indexes or copy artifacts unless their generation workflow explicitly requires it.
- Persian UI is RTL and uses IRANYekan; use logical layout properties and natural Persian wording.
- Phone numbers, URLs, email, tokens, file paths, and code remain LTR and should not inherit Persian digit/font treatment blindly.
- Keep accessible labels meaningful; icon-only controls need localized names or tooltips.
- Put product names, URLs, and logo paths in `skyroom-layout/white-label.js`, not scattered replacements.
- Avoid new DOM-wide text rewriting. Prefer source messages or server settings.
- Check interpolation, plurals, long labels, narrow mobile widths, and mixed Persian/Latin content.
- This meeting client uses styled-components and scoped CSS; do not apply Ant Design/Tailwind rules from Meeting-Panel.
